course: dictionary
lesson: 4030
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as 1), 2) and 3). To pick the right one, read the words around it. «Early cars had open tops and roads were mostly dust and stones, so motorists wore goggles, caps, gauntlets (long gloves) and long dust coats.» The clues are open tops, dust and stones, so a gauntlet here is a glove.
explain: Knights wore a gauntlet too, but a different one: a metal glove that was part of their armour. The meaning changes again in phrases. A knight who threw down a gauntlet was challenging an enemy to a fight. Here the phrase means something different from the single word on its own.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If «throw down the gauntlet» meant dropping a glove on the floor, the sentence would not make sense. Always ask whether your first idea still fits.
fact: A gauntlet is a thick glove with a long, wide cuff that covers the wrist.
fact: Early motorists wore gauntlets to keep off the cold and the dirt.
fact: A knight's gauntlet was a metal glove, part of his armour.
fact: «Throw down the gauntlet» means challenge someone; «take up the gauntlet» means accept a challenge.
fact: «Run the gauntlet» means face attacks or criticism from many people one after another.
exercise: «In front of the Hall stands a huge shiny red car, and down the steps swaggers Toad in goggles, cap, gaiters, gauntlets and an enormous overcoat.» What is a gauntlet in this sentence? | *A thick glove with a long, wide cuff | A metal glove from a knight's armour | A type of car | A kind of hat
exercise: «Sam threw down the gauntlet and asked Lee to a race.» What does threw down the gauntlet mean? | *Challenged Lee to a race | Gave Lee a present | Dropped a glove on the floor | Ran away from the race
exercise: «The new girl had to run the gauntlet of teasing on her first day.» What does run the gauntlet mean? | Win every game | *Face criticism or attacks from many people one after another | Run very fast across a field | Wear gloves in the cold
test: «Early motorists wore gauntlets against cold and dirt.» Which meaning of gauntlet fits here? | *A thick glove with a long, wide cuff | A type of motor car | A challenge to a fight | A metal glove from a knight's armour
test: Mia says, «I will take up the gauntlet and enter the spelling bee.» What does take up the gauntlet mean? | Put on a pair of gloves | Give up on the contest | *Accept the challenge | Lose a glove at the bee
exam: Which sentence uses gauntlet to mean a challenge? | Dan wore his gauntlets to the beach on a cold day | Dan's gauntlet was made of shining metal and kept in a glass case | Dan pulled on his gauntlets before he chopped the logs | *Dan threw down the gauntlet and challenged the champion to a chess match
